{
 "On the day of the sitting, the conciliator may meet the parties separately and jointly, and may formulate terms of settlement on the basis of the proposals received.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A settlement reached at the sitting shall be recorded as a settlement agreement under <1>Section {0}</1> or, in an arbitration, as an award on agreed terms. If no settlement is reached, the main proceeding shall continue, and nothing said or submitted at the sitting shall be relied upon in it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter XI</1>Mediation-Arbitration (Med-Arb) Protocol": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Initiation of Med-Arb Hybrid Proceedings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Med-Arb Protocol applies where the parties have agreed, before or after a dispute has arisen, to resolve the dispute by mediation followed, if settlement is not reached, by arbitration under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Med-Arb under this Code is of two kinds: (a) Same-Neutral Med-Arb, in which the person appointed as mediator continues, if the mediation fails, as the sole arbitrator; and (b) Separate-Neutral Med-Arb, in which the mediator does not serve as arbitrator and the Institute appoints a different person to arbitrate.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "On registration of a Med-Arb proceeding, the Secretariat shall appoint a mediator and fix the period of the mediation phase, which shall not exceed sixty days unless the parties agree otherwise.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Transition from Mediation Phase to Arbitration Phase": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "If the dispute, or any part of it, is not settled by the end of the mediation phase, or if a party earlier declares in writing that the mediation has failed, the proceeding shall continue as an arbitration under this Code in respect of the unsettled issues.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The date of commencement of the mediation phase shall be treated as the date of commencement of the arbitration for the purposes of limitation, to the extent permitted by law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Dual Role of Neutral (Opt-In / Consent Requirements)": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The parties may choose, in their agreement or at any time before the mediation phase ends, either Same-Neutral Med-Arb or Separate-Neutral Med-Arb.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the agreement of the parties is silent on whether the mediator may act as arbitrator, the parties shall be deemed to have chosen Same-Neutral Med-Arb, and the mediator shall continue as the sole arbitrator in the arbitration phase, so that the arbitrator is acquainted with the negotiations that took place in the mediation phase.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In Separate-Neutral Med-Arb, the Institute shall appoint as arbitrator a person other than the mediator, in accordance with the appointment provisions of this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "By choosing, or being deemed to have chosen, Same-Neutral Med-Arb, each party agrees that the mediator may act as arbitrator in the same dispute and waives any objection to the arbitrator's appointment on the ground only of the arbitrator's earlier role as mediator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Protection of Information Disclosed in Mediation Phase": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In Separate-Neutral Med-Arb, no information disclosed in the mediation phase, and in particular no information given in a private session, shall be placed before the arbitrator or relied upon in the arbitration phase, save with the consent of the party that disclosed it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In Same-Neutral Med-Arb, the arbitrator may take into account the course of the negotiations in the mediation phase; but, so that each party may answer the case against it, the arbitrator shall, before the arbitration phase begins, disclose to all parties the substance of any confidential information received in private session which the arbitrator considers material to the dispute, and shall not rely on any such information that has not been so disclosed.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Consent Awards Resulting from Med-Arb Settlements": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the parties settle in the mediation phase, or in the arbitration phase, the settlement shall, at their request, be recorded by an arbitrator appointed for the purpose as an arbitral award on agreed terms under Section {0} of the Act, having the same status and effect as any other arbitral award.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter XII</1>Specialized Corporate ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter XIII</1>Implementation and Enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The parties undertake to carry out every award, order, and settlement under this Code without delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "At the request of a party, the Institute shall provide implementation support, which may include computation of the sum due with interest and costs, a structured demand for compliance, facilitation of negotiated compliance, identification of assets and of the appropriate forum for execution, and coordination of execution proceedings.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Institute supports the implementation of awards and settlements throughout the world. On the request of a party, the Secretariat shall furnish certified copies of the award and the arbitration agreement, certified translations, and such certificates as to the conduct of the proceeding as may be required for recognition and enforcement of the award in another country under the New York Convention.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where a party so requests, the Institute shall coordinate recognition and enforcement abroad through counsel in the country concerned, at the cost of the requesting party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter XIV</1>Costs & Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The tribunal and administrative fees shall be fixed on the basis of the claim. A counter-claim shall attract fees on the same pattern, as if it were an independent claim. For disputes that cannot be quantified, the Secretariat shall fix the fee having regard to the facts of the case.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The parties shall deposit the fees in the instalments set out in the Schedule of Fees, in equal shares unless the Schedule provides otherwise. Where the respondent fails to deposit its share, the claimant shall deposit it in order to continue the proceedings, subject to the final outcome of the matter.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral shall, in the award, determine the costs and which party shall bear them, in accordance with Section {0}A of the Act, and may apply (a) the loser-pays principle, (b) the principle of equal or proportional payment, or (c) the claimant-pays principle, as the neutral deems fit in the nature of the case, having regard to the conduct of the parties, including the extent to which each has conducted the proceeding in an expeditious and cost-effective manner, the outcome, and any offer of settlement.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter XV</1>Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where an agreement refers disputes to the Code of the Institute, or to the latest version of the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, without specifying an edition, the edition in force on the date of commencement of the proceeding shall apply.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Link to Section {0}A": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
